recv_comp_work_ctr_test - Test module for nordda recv_comp_work_ctr vs cancel_work_sync

Tests whether recv_comp_work_ctr in srv/nvmeibs_nordda.c is needed or if
cancel_work_sync alone suffices.

Behavior:
1. HR-timer simulates interrupt, schedules work on a WQ
2. Work checks global atomic "run_allowed"; prints error if it is 0
3. Main thread (module init) runs 1000 iterations:
   - Set run_allowed=1, start timer
   - Wait for timer to fire
   - Decrement run_allowed to 0
   - Call cancel_work_sync
   - Wait to observe any hazards
   - Set run_allowed=1, re-init work, continue

Build:
  make

Run (cancel_work_sync only - default, 100us interrupt rate):
  sudo insmod recv_comp_work_ctr_test.ko

Run (with recv_comp_work_ctr pattern like nordda):
  sudo insmod recv_comp_work_ctr_test.ko use_ctr=1

Run (faster interrupt rate, e.g. 50us for ~20k/sec):
  sudo insmod recv_comp_work_ctr_test.ko timer_fire_us=50

Run (cross-CPU: timer on CPU 1, main thread on CPU 0 - default):
  sudo insmod recv_comp_work_ctr_test.ko

Run (same-CPU, timer_cpu=-1):
  sudo insmod recv_comp_work_ctr_test.ko timer_cpu=-1

Unload:
  sudo rmmod recv_comp_work_ctr_test

Check results in dmesg:
  dmesg | tail -20

If hazard_count > 0, work ran with run_allowed=0 (race detected).
